    ; that init allocates its buffer through `Page.get(this)`, and for a
    ; temporary the compiler may place on the stack the resulting `data`
    ; pointer is garbage. The name then compares unequal to everything and
    ; every property reads back as unknown — measured, and invisible until
    ; the first lookup.
